  "notes": [
    "Regional site overlay (ADR 0042) for the sacred grove (hiis) in May 1343: old oaks, lindens and ash on a low rise, cup-marked offering stones under them, a spring at the foot of the rise by the river, a meadow below and spruce and birch forest round it. No human building stands here.",
    "Invented composite (docs/LOCATIONS/sacred_grove.md, history/dossiers/folklore/harju-hiis-sites-within-walk-1343.md): sacred groves are attested, this one is not. The terrain is EU-DEM at Kostivere (Joelahtme parish), a representative karst rise by the Joelahtme river south-east of Reval, chosen for the game; it claims nothing about Kostivere. Coordinates are metres from that origin, x east, y south.",
    "The river course is the OSM Joelahtme joegi (way 218280416), simplified; modern settlement, industry and ditches are not used. Points of interest of kind offering_stone and spring are dressed by the site script (scenes/world/sites/hinterland_site.gd)."
  ],
